{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1107811-how-is-this-short-story-for-my-vampire","id":1107811,"title":"How is this short story for my vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-25T17:05:44-07:00","id":1107811,"title":"How is this short story for my vampire?","content":"My game-master wants everyone to make a short story about there character, and something interesting(but with room for changes, etc...) so he can make a long Chronicle that he can set up as he goes(we trust our GM since he is a very good story maker who knows how to make up stuff as he goes)... the whole thing is basically just a big story about small group of medium-high generation vampires who met by pure coincidence who are helping each other out due to good chance of personal gain, or maybe they have some kindness left in their somewhat empty undead hearts(tho that last one is pure speculation, being a vampire game). Eventually we will move away from characters stories into a bigger plot(with some stuff taken from the character backstories and fit into one bigger tale), but that is going to be awhile from now.<br /> <br /> I am a bit of a sloppy writer, so I am asking for you guys to rate it based on how good it sounds, but tell me if I didn't leave enough room for anything unexpected(again as per my GM's request):<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> My Nosferatu was unwillingly part of an experiment by Clan Tremere who were developing a way to both remove the clan curse from Nosferatu and at the same time permanently brainwash them into doing service for the Tremere Clan as a whole without the need to trick them into blood-bonds or using high level disciplines so they could mass produce covert agents to help them keep eyes and ears on everything happening in the city without fear of being betrayed. My Nosferatu was one of few partially successful experiments, and only mostly cured of their clan curse(Basically a free &quot;rugged bad looks' merit, not a complete cure.), but was for a very long time a slave to the Clan Tremere for a long time, but my Nosferatu has gotten their free-will back since they by pure chance found an abandoned magical charm that specifically breaks mind-control of most forms.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately my Vampire has to unquestioningly do tasks for Clan Tremere still since if they find out they will probably &quot;fix&quot; the issue the hard way, but they do take any chance they can to get info about what they did to him when ts safe. So far my Vampire knows that Clan Tremere has been using Nosferatu as unwilling experiment subjects, but is trying to find evidence of the experiments(which has been pretty well hidden) so they can reveal it to his clan-mates.<br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Does that sound good at all for a character short story?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12956-devonh","name":"DevonH","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T20:07:03-07:00","id":1107859,"title":"","content":"Make it not the work of the whole Clan Tremere, but instead a relatively small project, perhaps by an Elder, perhaps by a Methuselah, maybe by an Ancilla. (The one behind the project does not neccesirely have to be a Tremere.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-25-2017, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T23:01:17-07:00","id":1107907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1107811-how-is-this-short-story-for-my-vampire?p=1107859#post1107859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it not the work of the whole Clan Tremere, but instead a relatively small project, perhaps by an Elder, perhaps by a Methuselah, maybe by an Ancilla. (The one behind the project does not neccesirely have to be a Tremere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>right. I will have to edit that. Tho one thing for sure is there is no way to tell exactly how big or small the group behind this is(at least not to the other players, besides the GM of course). Thanks for pointing that out! any other suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12956-devonh","name":"DevonH","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T02:03:09-07:00","id":1107946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DevonH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1107811-how-is-this-short-story-for-my-vampire?p=1107907#post1107907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> right. I will have to edit that. Tho one thing for sure is there is no way to tell exactly how big or small the group behind this is(at least not to the other players, besides the GM of course). Thanks for pointing that out! any other suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest to play up the &quot;No idea who did it, no clue who is involved.&quot; aspect of the situation; not only it is hard to gather evidence - even when some is found, it is disjointed, almost as if someone observing the search for evidence and playing with the ones searching for it; or the evidence could be weird/fragmentary because those doing it have bad organization and aren't <i>that</i> sure about what they are doing and what is actually possible? (Very likely considering how large in aim and scope the idea is.)<br /> It could very well be an idea given to Kindred by a Ghoul or a human, because it sounds so over-ambitious. It could be thus financed and the logistics set up by humans (maybe even deluded hunters or Hunters), which makes it all the more harder to track the Kindred responsible.<br /> It could have a Coterie behind it, or one or two Kindred. Maybe a Tremere, or maybe it's someone bold enough (or desperate enough?) to fake Tremere responsibility so as to put the suspicion on them?<br /> Maybe the Kindred behind the experiments, for safety reasons or other reasons, from time to time lose interest (or at least appear to lose interest) in continuing the experiments? Considering this involves Clan Nosferatu, the ones behind it would have to be careful about covering their tracks; yet at the same time some Nosferatu could be reluctantly supportive of the experiments, because of the possibility of restoring their appearance, or that of their future Childer.<br /> <br /> Someone working towards removing a Clan Curse could have attracted attention of one or more interested parties, who might be just observing, or might be actively meddling and manipulating the situation. Thus there could be the ones behind the experiments, and there could be others connected to the experiments and the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-26-2017, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T09:06:12-07:00","id":1108040,"title":"","content":"As sugestion you could add that one of the things he have found is that the curse-removing-thing has unexpected side effects on some subjects (perhaps they became even worse after a time or start to have frenzies more often or they just died). So your character doesn't know if he is part of that group and eventually is going to be back to normal (for a Nosferatu) and having some of that side effects.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of not knowing if the Tremere are doing it by their own or if it is the plan of a bigger group. Depending of who are the other players, it could be tied up in an interesting climax. But it is up to your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}